---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { docs, repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Architecture | OrbitKV"
  description="OrbitKV ABI6 identities, immutable snapshots, Prefix/COW transactions, reclamation, and engine boundaries."
  active="Architecture"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>One authority for snapshots, sharing, and reuse.</h1>
    <p>
      ABI6 compiles retention semantics into immutable request snapshots and
      generation-checked physical-page transactions.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Architecture" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Pipeline</h2>
      <pre><code>{`Attention / state retention semantics
    -> Retention IR
    -> Lifetime / head stripes
    -> LayoutProgram
    -> PhysicalPlan
    -> immutable SnapshotLease head
    -> tail / COW copy / write intents
    -> completion-gated publication
    -> detach + final-ref certificate
    -> backend ACK + reuse`}</code></pre>

      <h2>Generated layouts</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table-native">
        <thead><tr><th>Semantics</th><th>Layout</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Full</td><td><code>AppendOnly</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sliding</td><td><code>Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sink + Sliding</td><td><code>Pinned + Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Same Chunk</td><td><code>ResettableArena</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-head windows</td><td>Lifetime-normalized stripes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Logical identity is separate from physical slot and generation.</li>
        <li>Address programs are the only logical addressing authority.</li>
        <li>Reuse requires semantic death, reader completion, and backend commit.</li>
        <li>Unsupported semantics and engine contracts fail closed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>ABI6 manager lifecycle</h2>
      <p>
        A request points at an immutable, generation-checked snapshot head.
        <code>prepare_batch</code> keeps a candidate private and returns tail,
        exact COW copy, and fresh-write intents. <code>submit_batch</code>
        validates exact backend receipts. <code>complete_batch</code> publishes
        every request head atomically only after completion evidence validates.
      </p>
      <p>
        Request and Prefix refs, reader pins, and the writer live on the page.
        Detach returns explicit mirror CLEAR/REPLACE actions; a reclamation
        certificate appears only when the final ref is gone. Ambiguous copy,
        launch, or completion outcomes enter fail-stop quarantine.
      </p>

      <h2>Current integration boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The modular Rust core, exact 23-symbol C ABI6 wire, split Python
        FFI/runtime/plugin layers, and SGLang <code>OrbitKVPrefixCache</code>
        are host L2 GO. H20 Prefix correctness and performance remain pending.
      </p>

      <h2>Capability levels</h2>
      <p>
        OrbitKV reports compiler, host/ABI, GPU-primitive, engine-E2E,
        and production qualification separately. The{" "}
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>
          Capability Matrix
        </a>{" "}
        is the normative boundary.
      </p>

      <h2>Records</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        {docs.map((item) => (
          <div class="doc-card">
            <span>{item.key}</span>
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
            <a href={item.href}>Open record →</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Boundary.</strong>
        <p>
          The historical frozen 9233c06d ABI5-v5 snapshot has scoped Full/Hybrid L4
          correctness on one H20 against official SGLang v0.5.17. It does not
          qualify ABI6. Same-capacity memory reduction is 0%, and
          <code>performance_go</code> is false because the B4 measurements come
          from one epoch. ABI6 H20 Prefix E2E, relocation, Graph/overlap,
          speculation, multi-GPU, and disaggregation remain unqualified.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>
          Current capability matrix
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
